    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as our clear focal point, sporting a dominant 73.66 efficiency score. Facing Graham Holmes (4.71 xERA), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 17% boost due to the favorable opposing arm and an additional 14% cushion from a strong platoon advantage, making him our highest-upside asset for runs and RBI. Alongside him, **Drake Baldwin** (58.61), **Jacob Wilson** (58.31), and **Heliot Ramos** (58.59) form a robust core of strong starts. **Jacob Wilson** is particularly well-positioned, utilizing a 10% park factor boost to help mitigate the challenge of facing Sonny Gray, while **Heliot Ramos** remains a priority start despite a neutral matchup, as his 50% SB probability keeps him in play for our desperate need for speed.\n\nOur most difficult decision revolved around the bottom of the outfield rotation and our utility spot. **Luis Robert Jr.** (48.05) narrowly missed a higher tier of recommendation; while his 88% SB frequency against the slow delivery of Eu-Yi P\u00e9rez is a significant asset, his performance is currently hamstrung by a 15% penalty from the platoon disadvantage. Meanwhile, **Miguel Vargas** remains a marginal play at 44.53; his 20% SB hold provides moderate floor support, but he is forced into a tough matchup against Ryan Weathers. As we monitor the lineups, we remain cautious of the volatility surrounding **Liam Hicks** (43.30), whose value is currently depressed by a 14% penalty against McLean\u2019s skill set. With **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** off today and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the volume of our active starters to navigate the scarcity of this 5x5 landscape.",
